<h1>Aboriginal Science Fiction Listings</h1>
<p>
Five years after the demise of <i>Galileo</i>, Charles C. Ryan started
<i>Aboriginal</i>. The magazine suggests that the actual publisher is
"A Crazy Alien" (who contributes editorials to each issue), and that
the target audience for the magazine is the aboriginal natives currently
inhabiting Earth.
<p>
Like <i>Omni</i> and the later <i>Science Fiction Age</i>, <i>Aboriginal</i>
was printed entirely on slick paper, with each story accompanied by a full-page
illustration. The magazine nearly died in 1995, but has managed to publish
an average of 2 issues per year since then.
